      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm fully against this, let people do what they want in their own instances, they can break all the rules anyways with custom avatars. You can make flying avatars, you can place sticker-like content with custom avatars, you can easily make own emojis with custom avatar, so such license/agreement was never valid in the first place so the whole argument just feels invalid at this point.\n\nFor any commercial events they have official public/group instances where everything is moderated, no need to try to limit what people do in own instances that random people can't access anyways.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
